    "It was three days, by four Eyes. On the third night the sky ahead of them turned orange and stayed that way."
    "The Kessler Banks had been islands once. They were low and sandy and so thoroughly built over that it was no longer possible to say where one stopped and the next began. There was a sound, too, a steady ringing roar. It was fifty thousand hammers."
    "Three hundred thousand people lived in Keelhaven, and the city kept no clocks. It kept sirens. One sounded as they came in past the breakwater, a long rising howl. On every gantry the small figures put down their tools, and others came up the ladders to take their places."

    show p wrack_assured_calm as left at head_left
    with qd
    c_ilan "Six shifts a day,"
    c_ilan "They name the hours by them. {i}I'll see you at third siren.{/i} I lived here two years, when I was learning hulls."

    hide left
    with qd
    "He could feel the ships on the slips through the Thread, faintly. They were not Maker work, and they did not answer. But there were Maker things in them."
    "Kessler-Vane bought every scrap the wreckers could tear out of the drowned ruins, and put it into its hulls without understanding it. He could feel those pieces, scattered through the yards like teeth coming in."

    show p wrack_assured_attentive as left at head_left
    with qd
    c_ilan "Slip Nine,"
    c_ilan "The big one."

    hide left
    with qd
