    with qd
    c_enginewoman "I've got a lamp,"
    c_enginewoman "At home. In the wall, behind the stove. I've had it nineteen years. My husband thinks it's a piece of drainpipe."
    show p wrack_assured_calm as left at head_left
    with qd
    c_ilan "Bring it,"

    hide left
    hide right
    with qd
    "She went and fetched it, there and then, through the patrolled streets, wrapped in a shawl. It was a hand lamp, a small one, such as the Makers must have carried about. He did not mend it."
    "He put it into her hands, and laid Jef's tool in her fingers, and showed her where the seam was. He told her what she was looking for. It took her forty minutes. He did not touch it once."
